# Master for the layout neighborhood tests (111, 112).
# Five chains with the same flow A -> B -> C, drawn in the four
# combinations of arrow direction, plus one joined by a layout
# constraint. Anchored at A with span 2, the layout neighborhood
# stops where the drawing turns (chains 2 and 3), the stream
# neighborhood never does, and neither follows the constraint.

process A1 A1
process B1 B1
process C1 C1
process A2 A2
process B2 B2
process C2 C2
process A3 A3
process B3 B3
process C3 C3
process A4 A4
process B4 B4
process C4 C4
process A5 A5
process B5 B5
process C5 C5

A1 --> B1
B1 --> C1

A2 --> B2
C2 <-- B2

B3 <-- A3
B3 --> C3

B4 <-- A4
C4 <-- B4

A5 --> B5
B5 >> C5
